    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d401">

                <pb facs="0493" n="381" sameAs="frus:frus1919Russia/pg381"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">861.01/69a: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the Commission to
                        Negotiate Peace</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1919-06-19T17:00:00-04:00"><hi rendition="#italic">June 19, 1919,
                                5 p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>2343. For the Secretary of State.</p>
                <p>Is Department to understand that acceptance of Kolchak’s reply<anchor n="6"
                        xml:id="d401-f1"/> merely means continuation of present relations with
                    Kolchak Government or does it convey <hi rendition="#italic">de facto</hi>
                    recognition and further and open extension of support along all lines
                    available?</p>
                <pb facs="0494" n="382" xml:id="pg382"/>
                <p>Press reports from Paris leave public in doubt on this question. Secretary of War
                    anxious to know whether he should change instructions to General Graves.<anchor
                        n="7" xml:id="d401-f2"/></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Polk</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d401-f1" n="6" xml:id="d401-f1-content">
                <p>Appendix I to C. F. 62, enclosure to Notes of Meeting on June 12, 4 p.m., <ref
                        target="#pg379">p. 379</ref>.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d401-f2" n="7" xml:id="d401-f2-content">
                <p>For reply see telegram from the Commission to Negotiate Peace, no. 2794, June 25,
                    12 p.m., <ref target="#pg386">p. 386</ref>.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
